0 !BRICK_STATE {"schema_version":3,"status":"instruction_reconstruction_in_progress","model":"Triceratops fossil reconstruction","reference_set":"LEGO 77985","reference_url":"https://www.lego.com/cdn/product-assets/product.bi.core.pdf/6649862.pdf","manual_files":["6649862-1.pdf","6649862-2.pdf"],"progress_note":"Step-278 link geometry is physically represented in its own submodel: 32140, 32184, and two 11214 geometry candidates. Their 40-LDU hole spacing and shared axes align; axial engagement segments are registered from official DAT dimensions. A provisional black 6541 receiver was added from the earlier step-247 body callout and aligned to the remaining 32140 hole with zero transverse axis residual and touching faces. Step-247 part identity fits the single-hole silhouette, but its use as the step-279 mating receiver and the local transform remain unverified. The skull datum and global skull/body transform are still unresolved.","piece_count":41,"unique_sale_skus":7,"listed_retail_parts_cost_cny":"0.95","cost_scope":"Not totaled; candidate mappings only.","target_dimensions_cm":{"length":null,"height":null,"width":null},"reference_geometry_bounds_cm":{"length":null,"height":null,"width":null},"support_count":0,"support_verification":"Not assessed.","validation":{"instruction_scope":"printed page 142 step 263; printed pages 143–148 steps 264–278; printed page 149 step 279: anterior torso receiver search and skull docking callout inspected","placements":"Step-278 link has exact official-DAT local registration, but manual part-number mapping remains candidate-level. 32140/32184 paired centerlines have 0 LDU transverse residual, 20 LDU face gap, and 11214 axle/pin intervals register. The third 32140 hole is provisionally aligned to 6541 from step247, while 32184 orthogonal cross-hole remains the skull-side port candidate; receiver contact has coaxial axes and touching faces, but callout identity/transform and a connecting pin are unverified. Mesh collision not tested.